## ⏱ LATEST DELTA — 2026-09-15 (Tue from `date`) (**#273**, ONE DAY, conductor **Fable** + **4 OPUS LANE SEATS** (roles-drift ×2 · list-vs-card · when-registry) with this **OPUS 5** wrap sub, DELEGATED — ★★★ **THE ADDRESS AND THE REGISTRY: FOUR RULINGS, 84 SILENT METAS GOT AN ADDRESS, AND THE `when` VOCABULARY BECAME A REGISTRY**)

*(WHY/HOW: the arc is one question asked twice. #270 and #271 both reported the same drift — `roles.json` claims 108 memberships and only 24 component metas carry `provides` — and both deliberately declined to fix it inside a landing. #273 is the session that went and fixed it, and the interesting part is what happened on the way: the drift page put four choices to Dave, he took three in one click and refused the fourth with a sentence about the future rather than the present, and the exploration that sentence licensed produced the session's most durable ruling — that a closed list of `when` field names is a REGISTRY, not a whitelist. Underneath both sits a red nobody had seen: #272's fifteen inscribed `when` predicates used thirteen field names that no registry contained, a resolver was never run, and a green `_validate_kg.py` had been reported in its place. The day is six commits and four rulings, and every enactment went in by textual span. Full narrative: `_DECISION-HISTORY/2026-09-15-273-the-address-and-the-registry.md`.)*

- ⛔★★★ **READ `_HANDOFF-124-the-address-and-the-registry.md` FIRST — IT IS NEWER THAN `_CHAIN.md` AND THEREFORE OUTRANKS IT.** The #273 conductor wrote it at **FILL ≈191,000 real — PAST the 180,000 working line and INSIDE the ~220,000 TOLERATED band whose arm this very session enacted — BEFORE this ritual ran**, so nothing in it depends on a delegated wrap remembering it. It carries his sentences verbatim, six commit receipts, an explicit DO-NOT-RULE list and #274's first moves; their source of record is `notes/_lanes/273/DAVE-RULINGS-2026-09-15.md`.

- ★★★ **FOUR RULINGS, `knowledge/_rulings.json` 562 → 566 — AND THE FIRST OF THEM IS AN ENACTMENT OF SOMEONE ELSE'S.** `s272-D93` had been a posture the machine never read; Dave's opener was two words — *"1. advisory arm"* — and `4294b60` wired it: `gauge.TOLERATED_TK = 220_000`, `STOP_LINE_TK` **180,000 UNCHANGED**, `_checkin.py`'s budget line now says TOLERATED between the two figures and PAST TOLERANCE above, driven at 170K / 195K / 220K / 230K with an 8/8 selftest block. ⛔ **The walls were not touched and no arm was made to block** — advisory is his word, not an inference.

- ★★★ **`s273-D1` — THE ADDRESS IS WRITTEN: 84 SILENT METAS NOW SAY WHICH ROLE THEY PROVIDE.** His export (`notes/_lanes/273/roles-drift/roles-drift-decisions-2026-09-15.json`) came back **RD-1 a · RD-2 a · RD-4 a**, inscribed as `s273-D1`…`s273-D3`. The enactment at `0d98a34` ran `knowledge/_enact_s273_d1_address.py` — `provides` written onto **84 metas BY TEXTUAL SPAN, reconstruction-proven per file** — and the drift the last three sessions reported reads **108/108 agree, 0 silent, 0 roles at zero**. `gen_kg_roles_desk.py --land --ratified s270-D2` then took `providesRole` from **24 → 108** across **207 edges / 85 metas**, `_validate_kg.py` OK, explorer regenerated. ⚠ **DECLARED IN THE SAME BREATH:** the regen rewrote Chart-boxplot's `yieldsTo` `$note` and **dropped a hand-added `span.cols` sentence** — the field is generator-owned, so if that sentence mattered it belongs on the meta; the loss is named rather than discovered later.

- ★★★ **`s273-D4` — THE `when` FIELD LIST IS A REGISTRY, NOT A WHITELIST, AND THE ROUTE TO IT IS THE BEST THING IN THE SESSION.** RD-3 came back **null** with his note verbatim — *"I need to understand the implications of this, maybe closing the list was a bad idea, I have a feeling this will reoccur, lets explore"* — so the conductor explored three fence shapes instead of asking again, and his answer to those was *"1. is thsi a candidate for an N-gram? probably over engineering"*. ⇒ **`knowledge/when-fields.json` stays the ONE home, the resolver still REFUSES an undefined name, and a lane MAY ADD a name with a definition and an example, listed in its report** — and **NO NEW INSTRUMENT WAS BUILT**: the existing advisory `_near_dupes.py` is pointed at the registry's definitions at verify time. `5f0c97f` defined the **13 names by textual span**, amended `$description` by addition, and took the resolver **FAIL(20) → FAIL(6)**.

- ⛔★★★ **THE RED THIS SESSION FOUND IS ABOUT WHAT WAS REPORTED, NOT WHAT WAS BUILT.** `_validate_roles_resolve.py` went **FAIL(6) → FAIL(20) at `b46ea90`** — #272's fifteen inscribed `when` predicates used **13 field names that existed in no registry**, across 9 metas, and the seam declared none of it because **`_validate_kg.py OK` was reported in the resolver's place and the resolver was never run**. ★ The class is the one this project keeps re-meeting: a green gate is only evidence about the gate that ran [[no-gate-parses-the-artefact]]. The remaining **FAIL(6) is #261's `data-grid` `with`-slugs, inherited and not new.**

- ★★★ **`s273-D3` PULLED `P-272-1` FORWARD AND THE RESEARCH SAYS THE LINE NOBODY DRAWS IS THE FIELD COUNT.** On his *"If the list vs card blocks anything lets do that too"* the LIST-vs-CARD lane ran in parallel (`783a8d9`, `notes/_PROPOSAL-list-vs-card-2026-09-15-v1.html`): **13 external systems, 0 of them draw the boundary on how many fields a row carries**; the three predicates that ARE load-bearing are **surface · record-level actions · same-shape set**, and **GOV.UK's summary card is the one genuine list-card precedent**. ★ The lane also **corrected its own brief**: `cards` DOES provide `arrangement`, and only `account-card` is `$not-a-provider`. ⛔ **LC-1…LC-4 ARE ON THE PAGE AND NOT ONE IS RULED** — LC-1 (option a) would need exactly one new field, `actions`.

- ⬛ **STILL HIS, AND EXPLICITLY NOT RULED AT THIS WRAP — the handoff's DO-NOT-RULE list, carried word for word:** **LC-1…LC-4** on the list-vs-card page (the line · the shapes · account-card) — **`P-272-1`'s owner is Dave** · the **`example` key** on the 13 new `when-fields.json` entries, which the **26 legacy entries lack** (declared, his) · the **4 near-dupe pairs** (`records`/`rows` · `entry`/`content` · `exits`/`destinations` · `steps`/`parts`) · the **6 `data-grid` `with`-slug reds** (#261) · the **`input` sub-roles** (27 providers, `$extension`) · **`P-272-2`…`P-272-4`** · and everything in handoff-123's list not named here. ⚠ **`P-272-1` and `P-272-2` TRIPWIRES FIRED AT THIS WRAP** (`_parked.py --check`) because `s273-D1` touched `list-items.meta.json` and `modals.meta.json` in the mass `provides` pass — **a mechanical fire, not a decision, and neither sidequest advanced.**

